@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title opencode paradigm — subagent crew with HITL oversight

actor "Developer\nreviews between loops" as DEV

node "opencode container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh" as EP <<app>>
  component "opencode TUI / run --auto" as CLI <<app>>

  frame "Seeded crew (~/.config/opencode/agents)" as CREW <<host>> {
    component "plan\nread-only: edit+bash denied" as PLAN <<app>>
    component "build\nedit allow · bash ask" as BUILD <<app>>
    component "reviewers\nadversarial · security · spec-keeper" as REV <<app>>
  }

  component "native LSP\nauto-enabled per detected language" as LSP <<app>>
  artifact "AGENTS.md" as MD <<db>>
  database "/app — repo (rw, .git rw)" as WS <<db>>
}

DEV ARROW_MAIN CLI
EP ARROW_MAIN CREW : seed missing only\n(""OPENCODE_RESEED=1"" forces)
EP ARROW_MAIN MD : seed when absent
EP ARROW_MAIN LSP : detect workspace languages
EP ARROW_MAIN CLI : " ""OPENCODE_MODEL"" · ""OPENCODE_BUILD_MODEL"" \n""OPENCODE_SMALL_MODEL"" (provider-prefixed) "
CLI ARROW_MAIN BUILD : implement
BUILD ARROW_MAIN WS
CLI ARROW_OPTIONAL PLAN : specs and step lists
BUILD ARROW_QUEUE REV : review loop
REV ARROW_MAIN DEV : findings surface to the human

note right of CREW
  **Roles are structural, not advisory.** The plan agent
  has ""edit"" and ""bash"" set to deny and reviewers are
  read-only, so "don't change code while reviewing" is a
  permission, not a prompt instruction.

  ""build"" keeps ""bash: ask"" — the HITL point.
end note

note bottom of EP
  Model ids are **provider-prefixed** here
  (""anthropic/claude-…""); ""apply_env_bridges"" normalizes a
  bare id and fills the small slot from ""EDITOR_MODEL""
  first, ""SMALL_MODEL"" second — the one harness whose
  tier mapping differs
  (_spec/internal/entrypoint/model-alias-bridges.puml).

  Supports ""--local-model"" (Ollama sidecar, litellm-free
  OpenAI-compatible endpoint) and DinD.
end note
note bottom of CLI
  **Narration is split across three switches, and one of them is unsafe on
  the TUI path.** ""--log-level DEBUG"" records what the harness did;
  ""--print-logs"" puts that on stderr, which only works when the TUI is not
  drawing on the same terminal, so off the TUI path it stays in the log
  file instead. On ""run"", ""--thinking"" keeps the model's reasoning blocks in
  the transcript rather than collapsing them — the closest opencode comes
  to showing its thoughts — and it has to be inserted before the prompt
  argument.
end note


@enduml
